  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want the \"Stockage MP\" settings to show one switch per thing it does, each with a short explanation, so that I understand what MPStorage is for and turn on only what I want (for example « MP multiples → dark topic »).\n\n### Requested (operator, 2026-11-12)\n- A clearer \"Stockage MP\" area, with **one switch per function** that MPStorage enables, including a switch **« MP multiples → dark topic »** (#858). « Dark topic » is the community's word for a non-public topic held in a group MP (operator, 2026-11-12): the switch makes group MPs behave as close as possible to a public topic.\n- An **info bubble** on the settings to explain them.\n\n### Today\n- `App/SwiftHFR/MPStorage/MPStorageSettingsSection.swift`: one toggle \"Activer le stockage MP\" with the account's state, then \"Dernier accès\" and \"Resynchroniser\" (port of `AppSettingsView.swift` `mpStorageSection` `:534-545` @ 87fe0d1c, a single `mpstorage_active` switch, default off).\n- MPStorage's functions (HFR-PROTOCOL §3.3, one JSON document in a private MP shared with other HFR+ clients): `blacklist` (LOT-131, #221), `bookmarks` (LOT-132, #222), `mpFlags` (#858).\n\n### Proposal (to settle in the spec)\n- Section \"Stockage MP\", with a footer of one or two sentences on what MPStorage is: a private MP used as storage, shared with other HFR+ apps (no real pseudo or MP id shown).\n- Master switch \"Activer le stockage MP\" (today's, with its creation question, ADR 0013 §7), then, while on, one switch per function:\n  - « Liste noire partagée » (#221),\n  - « Favoris de messages » (bookmarks, #222),\n  - « MP multiples → dark topic » (#858): group MPs get a topic's reading experience (flag, reading position, \"not fully read\" mark).\n  Each row has an ⓘ button opening a short popover: what it does, what it stores in the MP, what turning it off does.\n- Default with the master switch on: every function on (legacy parity: legacy's single switch turns them all on).\n- A function switched off stops **this app** reading and writing that section; it **never deletes** the section, nor other clients' data in it (the document keeps other clients' keys, LOT-062 / `MPStorage.m:886, 908`).\n- A function whose lot has not shipped yet does not show its switch (no dead switch).\n- Per account, like the master state (ADR 0013 §7; scope of the new keys in the ADR 0013 matrix, decided in the spec).\n- Ledger: `gap-edit` of GAP-181 (the single legacy switch becomes per-function switches, a (b) evolution).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Réglages › Stockage MP, logged in, on: the master switch, \"Dernier accès\", \"Resynchroniser\", and the switches of the shipped functions, each with an ⓘ that opens its explanation (VoiceOver: the ⓘ reads « Plus d'infos sur … »).\n- Turning a function off: the app stops using that section (e.g. no MP flag written, flags not shown); a resync leaves the section intact in the document (test with a scripted transport).\n- Logged out: today's sentence. Dynamic Type AX: rows wrap, popovers readable.\n- Tests on the model rules (defaults, per account, off = no read/write of that section); shown to fail without the change.\n- Related: #858, #221, #222, LOT-130 (#220).\n\n### Decision (operator, 2026-11-14)\n\n- ezzz wants a short settings list; the operator keeps the per-function switches as the **experimental option « Stockage MP détaillé »** (`ExperimentalFeature.mpStorageSwitches`, #903).\n- Default (switch off): the single legacy switch « Activer le stockage MP ». Switch on: the three per-function switches, each with its ⓘ:\n  - Liste noire partagée (#221);\n  - Favoris de messages (#222);\n  - MP multiples → dark topic (#858).\n- The open PR is reworked onto #903: its code goes to `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/MPStorageSwitches/`, with `// EXPERIMENTAL(mpStorageSwitches, #859)` where it replaces the single switch. It keeps its ADR 0013 §7 edit, so cloud/orch merges it. M5, `experimental`.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
